WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.360
Let's go to Isaac from Ohio.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.910
Next, Isaac from Ohio, you're on the air.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.120
Oh, God.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.830
Hello, how are you?

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.830
Good.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:18.279
What can I do for you, so forgive me if this
is completely incorrect, because he's not

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:25.949
taking a single economic class or anything,
but I know that you're you're like a social

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:27.140
Democrat.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.380
You're not in favor of, like, full blown socialism.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.380
Right.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.000
But I came up with an idea a little while
back.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.860
What if.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.480
Instead of like outlawing like capitalism
to go to socialism, because that would be

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.900
too complicated, it's like I don't I don't
know what if we take.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:56.790
What if we, like, defined like wage slavery
properly and outlawed that, like you couldn't

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:02.130
just like the common practice of just hiring
someone, paying them a flat rate for their

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:08.100
labor where they have no ownership of their
workplace, if we like, at least gave workers

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.479
some ownership of their workplace in all cases.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:16.759
So you're saying that with some kind of some
kind of law that says every employee must

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:20.329
be given partial ownership of their place
of employment?

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:22.929
Yeah, I don't see how you get that done legally.

00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:26.829
I mean, I don't I don't even know that it's
I think that the way to do it.

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:29.959
So that would be a very authoritarian imposition.

00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:36.439
And check out my interview with the with the
YouTube or Vash, who is a socialist.

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:42.179
But he said that the way that as he sees it,
the way you're going to implement these things

00:01:42.179 --> 00:01:48.369
is going to be by convincing businesses and
others that it's a good idea for them to do

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:53.649
it rather than imposing it as law, that I
hope I'm not wrong in summarizing his perspective

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:54.649
that way.

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:58.399
But even he said that the types of things
you're talking about are very authoritarian

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:02.259
and would essentially be dead ends.

00:02:02.259 --> 00:02:03.679
And I think that he's probably right about
that.

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:07.399
I think what you're suggesting would be very
would essentially be impossible to do.

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:12.540
You would just be saying you would be mandating
you are trying to force companies to do things

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.810
that there's no legal basis to force them
to do.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.310
It's less about economics, it's more about
the law.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:28.330
OK, so you're not particularly against something
like that, you're just saying it's not realistically

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.860
possible.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:33.980
So as a as a social Democrat, I'm not in favor
of what you're describing.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:38.030
But for me, it's not even really the main
issue because it's just you're not going to

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:42.420
get it done in the way where there's just
a law passed and it says all employees are

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.420
now owners.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:51.730
Yeah, well, I'm not trying to make it that
simple, like what if if we say like the lowest

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:57.480
tier of workers have to own, like, at least
20 percent of the entire company collectively,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.400
is that something that could work or.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.150
I don't see I don't see how you get it passed.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.540
I mean, I think the more important thing would
be to for you to think about this less as

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.580
an economic thing.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.040
But more is a how do you how do you get what
is the legal structure where you could do

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.040
that?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.040
Where government could do that?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.160
Is it federal and is it state?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.660
And if it's one versus the other, how do you
actually do it?

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:17.950
And I just don't see it.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.600
I think if I were you, I would focus on how
you get it done rather than whether it's a

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.600
good idea.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.520
I just don't see how you how you ever get
that done.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:28.240
Oh, yeah, I see, that's a really good point,
no.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.040
All right, my friend, though, I appreciate
the call.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.040
Yeah, thank you.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.040
All right, pleasure.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:04:22.840
Let's take a couple of others, because there
are many people, many, many people who want

00:04:22.840 --> 00:05:04.150
to chat.

